+#### Max consecutive losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the most recently closed trades for a pair, and counts how many of them, in a row, resulted in a loss (a profit below `required_profit`, which defaults to 0.0). As soon as a winning trade is found (or there are no more trades to look at), counting stops - this is a genuine consecutive-loss streak, not a count of losses within a time window.
+
+If `trade_limit` or more losing trades occurred in a row, that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`), giving the strategy a break from a pair that isn't performing under current conditions.
+
+By default, this Protection also monitors trading across all pairs combined and will lock all pairs if the bot-wide consecutive-loss streak reaches `trade_limit` - set `only_per_pair` to true to only ever lock the specific pair that is on a losing streak.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+This Protection does not consider `lookback_period`, since it is only concerned with the most recent, unbroken streak of losses.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` is not set, the whole bot) for 4 candles after 3 losing trades occurred one after another.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
